  "summary": "The distinctive color shifts, texture, and aging characteristics of images produced with Polaroid SX-70 instant film.",
  "description": "Creates warm, often faded or magenta-shifted images with a soft, painterly quality and visible texture due to the unique chemical makeup and instability of SX-70 film; this occurs as the dyes continue to develop and degrade over time, creating unpredictable color shifts. Popularized by artists like Andy Warhol and Lucas Samaras, and later embraced by the alternative photography movement for its unpredictable, painterly qualities.",
